      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The group of 141 school-year children with bronchial asthma was examined. The condition of upper gastrointestinal tract was assessed. Gastroesophageal reflux disease was revealed in 94 children (66.7%). Dyspepsia, mucosal damage and changes of 24-hour pH monitoring data were more intensive in acute period of asthma and in children with severe asthma. Acid supression in the complex therapy of gastroesophageal reflux disease permited to minimise symptoms of dyspepsia and improve the pH monitoring data."},
